# entries — the ONE worklog file. Append lines anytime, then run:  worklog-run --yes
#   (logs untracked lines to Jira AND mirrors op:-tagged keys to OpenProject)
# Copy this file to ~/.config/worklog/entries (or name it ./entries in your
# working folder) and start logging. NEVER commit your real entries file —
# it is personal timesheet data and is .gitignored by default.
#
#   format: KEY DURATION [DATE] op:<wp_id>[:<activity>] COMMENT
#     COMMENT is ALWAYS the last part of the line; the op: tag sits right
#     before it, after the duration and optional date.
#
#     no op: tag           -> Jira only
#     op:<wp_id>           -> also mirrored to that OpenProject work package
#     op:<wp_id>:<activity>-> OP activity by name ('+' = space) or numeric id;
#                             omit -> OP server default
#     DURATION  3h | 90m | 1h30m | 1h 30m | 0.5d | 2w      (day = 8h, week = 40h)
#     DATE      Today | Yesterday | YYYY-MM-DD | full ISO timestamp
#     KEY       bare key (DEMO-421) or any Jira link containing one
#
# OpenProject activity ids differ per instance — check your OP Time & costs
# dropdown or GET /api/v3/time_entries/activities.
#
# --- examples ----------------------------------------------------------------
#   DEMO-421 1h Today op:65:Support #data architecture
#   SAMPLE-10516 2h Yesterday op:448:Testing UAT round 2
#   INFRA-5321 30m                              today 09:00, generic comment
#   DEMO-435 1h 51m 2026-09-18 op:73 Test (sit) regression pass
#   https://jira.example.com/browse/DEMO-421 45m op:65 review feedback
# --- your entries below ------------------------------------------------------
